# Ruby 0.49 (1994-07-18?) grammar: rb-int-puts subset over the R0 tokens.
# @version 1
# PARTIAL: parses only the rb-int-puts subset below; everything else is a parse error.
# source_ref: https://github.com/ruby/ruby/tree/v0_49
# source_sha: 200e0ee2fd3c1c006c528874a88f684447215524
# evidence: parse.y blob 0f4f6409342a8ea3300c5830e7a0ccde61abead7; keywords blob -; defs/keywords blob -; prism/config.yml blob -
# basis: reviewed against the tag's own syntax files. Tokens follow parse.y yylex() and kwtable; the grammar follows its compexpr/expr2/primary rules.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rb-int-puts subset (LANG80) as this release's yacc grammar admits it:
#
#   compexpr : exprs opt_term ;  exprs : /*none*/ | expr | exprs term expr
#   primary  : IDENTIFIER '(' call_args rparen | '(' compexpr rparen | literal
#   expr2    : expr2 '+' expr2 | expr2 '-' expr2 | expr2 '*' expr2
#            | expr2 '/' expr2 | '-' expr2 %prec UMINUS | primary
#
# There is no paren-less command call in this release: `puts 1 + 2` is a
# syntax error, and so is `puts(1\n)` (rparen is a bare ')'). The lexer drops
# a newline whenever it is in EXPR_BEG (after an operator, `(`, `,`, `;` or
# another newline), so NEWLINE is accepted in exactly those places.
#
# Rule names follow code/grammars/ruby/ruby.grammar so the CST keeps the
# shape the Ruby IIR compiler walks (LANG84 C8). This release has no
# ternary, range, logical or comparison operators inside the subset; those
# rules are single-child links kept only for that contract.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

program     = { NEWLINE } [ statement ] { terms statement } [ terms ] ;
terms       = ( SEMICOLON | NEWLINE ) { NEWLINE } ;
statement   = method_call ;
method_call = NAME LPAREN { NEWLINE } [ call_arg { COMMA { NEWLINE } call_arg } ] RPAREN ;
call_arg    = expression ;

expression  = ternary ;
ternary     = range ;
range       = logical_or ;
logical_or  = logical_and ;
logical_and = logical_not ;
logical_not = comparison ;
comparison  = shift ;
shift       = sum ;
sum         = term { ( PLUS | MINUS ) { NEWLINE } term } ;
term        = factor { ( STAR | SLASH ) { NEWLINE } factor } ;
factor      = NUMBER | LPAREN { NEWLINE } expression RPAREN | unary_minus ;
unary_minus = MINUS { NEWLINE } factor ;
